      "title": "Event-file finalization bypasses the new original-first-error wrapper",
      "evidence": "run() stores the first work/RPC failure in result[first_error], then unconditionally flushes/fsyncs/closes event_file in its finally block. An exception at lines450-452 exits run before return seal_outputs(...). Therefore seal_outputs cannot attach that result.first_error to this exception, and main emits getattr(error,first_error,None), which is None for the ordinary OSError.",
      "concrete_failure_path": "An original RPC timeout is caught and retained in result, actors are aborted, then parent-events.jsonl fsync raises EIO/ENOSPC. No owner-result has yet been written; outer stderr reports the later file error with first_error:null. The process fails closed but the original error provenance is lost.",
      "control_coverage": "The final-owner supplemental negative control invokes seal_outputs for a metadata reservation refusal. It does not call run or inject failure in the event_file finally block, so its pass cannot close this branch.",
      "required_change": "In a separately frozen revision, preserve/attach the original result.first_error across event_file flush/fsync/close failures too, retain cleanup/finalization diagnostics separately, and keep the same caps/no-extra-file/nonzero behavior. Do not alter revision002 in place.",
      "root_and_author_notified_before_seal": true
    }
  ],
